class:: CliffordMap
summary:: Trigger-driven raw Clifford attractor coordinates
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/DeJongMap, Classes/LatoocarfianMap

description::

Clifford attractors apply four independent parameters to coupled trigonometric functions, scattering points in complex, beautifully smeared clouds without a single central origin. Mathematically, this lack of strong central gravity means the state wanders continuously across the phase space in overlapping sine-like waves. Conceptually, it behaves like a set of constantly detuning, free-running LFOs, providing lush, continuously evolving control signals perfectly suited for ambient modulation, drone pitch drift, or granular synthesis parameters.

Implements code::x' = sin(a*y) + c*cos(a*x):: and code::y' = sin(b*x) + d*cos(b*y)::, a commonly used Clifford-attractor recurrence. Parameters remain mathematical coefficients.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, CliffordMap updates on edges and holds; unlike Stepper, it computes coupled trigonometric state.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::clifford-map-phase.png#The Clifford attractor at the documented defaults. x is horizontal and y is vertical; overlapping points make the more frequently visited regions darker.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on a rising edge.
argument:: a
Trigonometric coefficient in the x equation.
argument:: b
Trigonometric coefficient in the y equation.
argument:: c
Cosine weight in the x equation.
argument:: d
Cosine weight in the y equation.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate.
argument:: reset
Restore initial coordinates on a rising edge.
returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ CliffordMap.ar(Impulse.ar(700))[0] * 0.08 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(CliffordMap.kr(Impulse.kr(14))[1].linexp(-2, 2, 100, 3000), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

code::
// Evolving Ambient Drone
(
{
    var trig, coords, freq, sig, filt;
    trig = Impulse.kr(20); // Fast triggers for continuous-feeling modulation
    coords = CliffordMap.kr(trig);
    // Smeared sine-like oscillations detuning a lush pad
    freq = 100 + (coords[0] * 2);
    sig = Splay.ar(SinOsc.ar([freq, freq*1.01, freq*0.99, freq*2]));
    filt = LPF.ar(sig, coords[1].linexp(-2, 2, 200, 4000));
    filt * 0.1
}.play;
)
::




subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Clifford map: x-y phase portrait",
    [-1.6, 2.1], [-1.5, 1.7],
    { CliffordMap.kr(Impulse.kr(120)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(-1.6, 2.1).linexp(-1.6, 2.1, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(-1.5, 1.7).linlin(-1.5, 1.7, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::
